      "id": "SAT_p1_10_S01",
      "type": "function_evaluation_even_function",
      "question": "g(x) = ax² + 32. For the function g defined above, a is a constant and g(4) = 16. What is the value of g(−4)?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "32",
        "B": "48",
        "C": "−16",
        "D": "16"
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "explanation": "16a + 32 = 16 gives a = −1. g(−4) = −1(16) + 32 = 16 (g is even, so g(−4) = g(4))."
    },
